# uml quality entry Tool Spec (#93)

Purpose: native Windows invocation surface for the adjacent uml-viewer quality dispatch (ADR 0068). CRAP and mutation run through uml-viewer's standard tools (crapper / mutator Lua paths); this repository owns only the scope config, the pinned Lua environment and the preflight.

Upstream (adjacent checkout, ignored by git): `.uml-viewer/uml-viewer/scripts/uml-command.ps1`, `.uml-viewer/crapper`, `.uml-viewer/mutator`, installed by uml-viewer's `get-uml-viewer`. These repositories are read-only from this project.
Project wrapper: `lua tools/cli.lua uml <check|crap|mutate|ir|view> [args]` (package `tools/packages/uml_quality/`).

CLI contract:
- `check` runs the preflight only: exit 0 when everything resolves, 1 otherwise.
- `crap` / `mutate` run the preflight, then `pwsh -NoProfile -File .uml-viewer/uml-viewer/scripts/uml-command.ps1 <root> crap|mutate [args]` inside a cmd batch, and pass its exit code through unchanged.
- Valid results are decided by uml-viewer and published to `.uml-viewer/quality-result.json` (echoed after the run): crap `0` or `2`; mutate `0` or `3`. Exit 3 is a valid mutate result (surviving mutants), not "unavailable", and not a universal success code: crap 3 is a failure.
- Preflight failure exits 1 (never 3), prints `FAIL` lines, deletes any stale `.uml-viewer/quality-result.json` and starts no tool.
- Missing or unknown operation exits 2.
- The installer copies `uml` / `uml.ps1` into the repo root. They are ignored and are not the supported entry, because they inherit the user's `LUA_PATH`. The one exception is inside the companion started by `uml view` (below), which inherits the pinned environment.

`ir` contract (#99 / ADR 0070):
- Takes no extra arguments (exit 2 otherwise).
- Projects `arch_policy.project_uml_policy` from `tools/packages/arch_policy/policy.json`, then merges `:proposals` and `:omit` from the versioned override `docs/architecture.proposals.edn` (`packages.uml_quality.proposals`), and sets `:out "tmp/uml/monopoly.edn"`. The merge never writes back to `docs/architecture.md` or the guards.
- Override shape: one top-level map with only `:proposals` and `:omit`, each a vector, copied verbatim. A missing, empty or comment-only file means `[]` for both. Malformed EDN, any other key, a duplicate key or a non-vector value exits 1 with a `docs/architecture.proposals.edn (line N): ...` message. In that case `policy.edn` is not written and nothing is started.
- Preflight: PowerShell 7, the uml-viewer checkout, and no repo-root `examples/`. `uml-command.ps1 ir` prefers `examples/*.policy.edn` over `policy.edn`, so an `examples/` directory could shadow the generated file. A preflight failure exits 1 and writes nothing.
- Then it writes the repo-root `policy.edn` (ignored by git) and runs `pwsh -NoProfile -File .uml-viewer/uml-viewer/scripts/uml-command.ps1 <root> ir tmp/uml/monopoly.edn`, which calls upstream `uml-viewer.main.ir-generator <policy.edn> <out.edn>`. The exit code is passed through unchanged.

`view` contract (#99 / ADR 0070):
- Preflight: the same Lua checks as `check` (native `lua.exe`, project-cache rocks, module probe), PowerShell 7, the uml-viewer checkout with `uml-quality.json`, and Herdr 0.9.3. Herdr is looked up only at `%USERPROFILE%/.herdr/packages/standalone/releases/0.9.3-<x86_64|aarch64>-pc-windows-msvc/herdr.exe`, and `herdr --version` must print exactly `herdr 0.9.3`. PATH is not searched, because another Herdr version is often there. Nothing is downloaded or upgraded.
- A preflight failure exits 1 with `FAIL` lines and does not start the upstream launcher. It leaves `.uml-viewer/quality-result.json` alone.
- Then a cmd batch runs `pwsh -NoProfile -File .uml-viewer/uml-viewer/scripts/uml-command.ps1 <root> [args]` (args forwarded, e.g. `--restart`). The batch carries the pinned environment above (`runtime.view_env`), with the Herdr 0.9.3 directory first on `PATH`, ahead of the `lua.exe` directory. The variables are set only inside the child batch, so the parent process, the global Herdr and Lua setup and the read-only upstream checkout are unchanged. Upstream creates a fresh Herdr server per launch, and the environment flows down to the companion and its shells. The exit code is passed through unchanged.
- Window, companion, CRAP colouring and Herdr cleanup are verified manually on native Windows by the maintainer. They are not covered by the automated suite.

Dispatch precedence (owned by uml-viewer `scripts/uml-command.ps1`, recorded here): `operations` > `standardTools` > Clojure alias. The alias route is taken only when `deps.edn` exists and no `standardTools` is declared; with neither, the standard tools run with installed defaults. `uml-quality.json` declares `standardTools` only:
- `sourceRoots: ["src"]`: the whole `src/` tree is business code, the same scope as the retired crap4lua lane.
- `exclude: []` must stay declared. uml-viewer's mutation scope adapter wraps an absent `exclude` as `@($null)` and fails, so the empty array is part of the contract.
- No routing flags (`--root`, `--source-root`, `--exclude`, `--full-tree`, `--changed`, `--mutate-all`) in `crapperOptions` / `mutatorOptions`. uml-viewer rejects them.
- crap always runs `--full-tree`. The preflight validates the file with uml-viewer's own `Read-UmlQualityConfig`, `Get-UmlBusinessRoots` and `Select-UmlMutationTargets` (`probe_config.ps1`), not with a local re-implementation.

Pinned Lua environment (the false-green guard):
- The user tree `%APPDATA%\luarocks` also carries busted / luacov / luacov-reporter-lcov, and the user `LUA_PATH` points at it. A child that inherits it would "work" without the project cache.
- The child batch therefore sets `LUA_PATH(_5_4)` = repo root + `.toolcache/luarocks/share/lua/5.4`, `LUA_CPATH(_5_4)` = `.toolcache/luarocks/lib/lua/5.4`, empty `LUA_INIT(_5_4)`, and puts the native `lua.exe` directory first on `PATH` (crapper uses `shutil.which("lua")`).
- There is no `;;` default path. `luarocks.loader` must stay unresolvable, otherwise it would re-attach the user trees.
- The preflight runs `probe_lua_modules.lua` under that environment. Every required module (`busted.runner`, `luassert`, `luacov.runner`, `luacov.reporter.lcov`) and every file loaded while requiring them, C modules included, must resolve under `.toolcache/luarocks`.
- Rocks come from `foundation.bootstrap` into the project tree only: busted 2.3.0-1, luassert 1.9.0-1, luacov 0.17.0-1, luacov-reporter-lcov 0.2-0, all from luarocks.org with `--tree <project cache>`. There is no mirror, no copy from the user tree and no write to the user tree.

Python environment (crapper / mutator):
- Python 3.11+ (both pyprojects: `requires-python >=3.11`; deps `tree-sitter>=0.24`, `tree-sitter-language-pack>=0.7`).
- One venv per checkout, created by uml-viewer's documented commands:
  - `py -3 -m venv .uml-viewer\crapper\.venv`, then `.uml-viewer\crapper\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -e .uml-viewer\crapper`
  - the same for `mutator`.
- The preflight runs each venv's `python.exe -I` and requires the version >= 3.11 and the package imported from its own checkout (`.uml-viewer/<tool>/src`). It also requires mutator's `ensure_crapper()` to resolve crapper from `.uml-viewer/crapper/src`.

Outputs and version control:
- crapper writes `.metrics/crap.edn` and `target/coverage/lua/lcov.info`; mutator writes `.metrics/mutate/*.edn`.
- Following the upstream README, `.metrics/` is versioned: metrics produced by real `lua tools/cli.lua uml crap|mutate` runs are committed. Never hand-write or fabricate metric files. `.metrics/` is a whitelisted root entry (`test/guards/lib/root_whitelist_guard.lua`).
- `ir` outputs stay out of version control. The repo-root `policy.edn` is listed in `.gitignore` and not whitelisted by the root guard. `tmp/uml/monopoly.edn` sits under the ignored `tmp/`. The override `docs/architecture.proposals.edn` is versioned and allowlisted by the docs guard.
- `target/` (coverage intermediates) stays ignored, like `.uml-viewer/` and `uml-viewer-log.txt` (installer-maintained block at the end of `.gitignore`).

Known gaps (not part of #93's reduced scope):
- Real CRAP scoring, full-tree coverage and source mutation (#93 acceptance criterion 3) have not been executed. Per the 2026-10-14 maintainer scope reduction, only tool availability is verified.
- There is no `.busted` config at the repo root. crapper / mutator pick the Lua module root from the nearest `.busted` or rockspec, otherwise the project root, so a real run would use busted's default `spec/` pattern instead of this repo's `test/` layout. Wire this before running criterion 3.
- An isolated worktree uses its own real `.toolcache`, filled by bootstrap (`luarocks --tree <worktree>/.toolcache/luarocks`). Never use a junction, symlink or mirror of the main checkout's cache: installs would land in the shared cache and the link cannot be cleanly removed. Never use the user tree either.
